Tannin
Free Steam Play for Mac.

Tannin is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 (see LICENSE).

Tannin builds on the work of others. It downloads the following at install time,
checks each against a pinned SHA-256, and redistributes none of it:

- NotProton (https://github.com/NotProtonNot/NotProton), GPL-3.0.
  The Steam add-on, the Steam bridge (a port of Valve's Proton lsteamclient, which is
  under the Steamworks SDK license, and steam-helper, BSD-3-Clause), signatures and helpers.
  Files under Tools/ntdll-patch/ are taken from NotProton and remain under its license;
  one of them, shim32.S, carries a two-line correction of Tannin's (see UPSTREAM.md there).
  The per-game graphics layers use the add-on's own runner variants and plugins.

- winecx-gptk (https://github.com/frankea/winecx-gptk, from https://github.com/dappermint/winecx-gptk).
  A build of Wine from CodeWeavers' published CrossOver sources. Wine is LGPL-2.1-or-later.
  The same download carries the graphics layers Tannin offers beside Apple's:
  DXMT (https://github.com/3Shain/dxmt), zlib license;
  DXVK (https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk, in Gcenx's macOS build), zlib license;
  MoltenVK (https://github.com/KhronosGroup/MoltenVK), Apache-2.0.
  Tannin changes none of them. It marks DXMT's three files so that Wine loads them from its own folders.

- Steam client files, from Valve's own download servers. Copyright Valve Corporation.

- Seven game covers, shown across the top of the setup window: Metro Exodus, Fallout 4,
  Red Dead Redemption 2, Horizon Zero Dawn, Death Stranding, DOOM Eternal and
  Ratchet & Clank: Rift Apart. Each belongs to its publisher. They are fetched from Steam's
  public servers when the setup window first opens and kept in the Mac's caches. They are not
  part of Tannin or of this repository; Tannin itself holds three colours per cover and nothing
  else of them.

The Tannin app includes one piece of other people's software, unchanged:

- Sparkle (https://sparkle-project.org), which checks for and installs updates to Tannin.
  MIT license, with further notices for the code it includes; the full text is inside the app at
  Tannin.app/Contents/Resources/Sparkle-LICENSE.txt. The `tannin` command line tool does not use it.

Tannin never includes Apple's Game Porting Toolkit or D3DMetal. You download the toolkit
from Apple yourself and Tannin imports it after checking Apple's code signature.

